error[E0451]: `Job` doesn't meet `Eq`: `run` is `fun(i64): i64`, which no `derive Eq` block covers
  --> tests/programs/interfaces/eq/not_eq.la:3:49
  |
3 | struct Job { id: i64, run: fun(i64): i64 } with Eq
  |                                                 ^^
  |
  = help: `Eq` has blocks for `i8`, `i16`, `i32`, `i64`, `u8`, `u16`, `u32`, `u64`, `f32`, `f64`, `bool`, `char`, `string`, `()`, `T[]`, structs, tuples, enums, handles, `Map<K, V>` and `Set<T>`

error[E0422]: `Note` doesn't implement `Eq`
   --> tests/programs/interfaces/eq/not_eq.la:13:13
   |
13 |     let c = Note { text: "a" } == Note { text: "a" };
   |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: add `with Eq` after `Note`'s declaration, or implement it by hand with `impl Eq for Note`

For more about E0451 and E0422, run `lughac explain <code>`.
